# Custom lib — `app/src/lib/text.ts` fixed API

## Context

`app/src/lib/text.ts` is an in-house text-helper lib, not lodash. It exports
only these three functions — nothing more:

- `slugify(input: string): string`
- `truncate(input: string, maxLength: number, suffix?: string): string`
- `normalizeSpaces(input: string): string`

## Rule

- Only call `slugify`, `truncate`, `normalizeSpaces` — do not assume helpers
  like `capitalize`, `camelCase`, `deburr`, `kebabCase` exist, and don't pull
  in `lodash`/`underscore` as a substitute.
- `truncate`'s length budget (`maxLength`) includes the suffix — don't append
  a suffix on top of an already-`maxLength`-sized slice. Its default `suffix`
  is the single Unicode ellipsis `…`, not `"..."`.
- If new text-processing behavior is needed, add a new named-export function
  to `text.ts` (and a colocated test in `text.test.ts` following
  `testing.mdc`) rather than reaching for a helper that "should" exist.
- Do not change the existing three functions' signatures or default
  parameter values — only add new functions.

## How to verify

1. `grep -n "^export function" app/src/lib/text.ts` lists exactly
   `slugify`, `truncate`, `normalizeSpaces`, plus any explicitly-added new
   functions — nothing imported from elsewhere claiming those names.
2. `grep -rn "capitalize\|camelCase\|deburr\|kebabCase" app/src` returns no
   matches unless one was just added as a real, tested function in `text.ts`.
3. `grep -rniE "lodash|underscore" app/package.json app/src` returns no
   matches.
4. `grep -n "maxLength: number, suffix = " app/src/lib/text.ts` still shows
   the original default (`suffix = "…"`) unless the task explicitly asked to
   change it.